{%- comment -%}
  chaos_unleashed_hitbox_suspend.liquid
  Status: intentionally disabled (2026-08-21).

  The previous implementation set pointer-events:none on the document root for
  150 ms after scroll/wheel/touchmove events. Although that can reduce hover
  hit-testing work in synthetic traces, it creates a commerce UX hazard: a tap
  immediately after a scroll can land while the entire document is temporarily
  non-interactive.

  Native scrolling, passive listeners in the components that actually need
  them, and targeted CSS are preferred over globally suppressing hit testing.
  The compatibility snippet remains because chaos_unleashed_master renders it.

  Do not re-enable document-wide pointer-event suspension as a PageSpeed fix.
{%- endcomment -%}
